diagnosis_text:
A complete, layered investigation of the live lab found no fault at any layer. Phase 1 reachability showed 0% packet loss from all sampled sources to all sampled destinations. Phase A infrastructure sweep (infra_sweep + l2_snapshot) confirmed zero ACL/firewall drop rules, zero static ARP poisoning, correct IP/gateway/resolver configuration on both hosts, and no duplicate MAC addresses anywhere in the topology. Phase B confirmed the OSPF/FRR control plane is fully healthy: all six FRR routers have active ospfd processes and full vtysh connectivity, all OSPF adjacencies are in the Full state, and every router carries 10 routes; tc_snapshot found no traffic shaping or corruption rules on any interface. Phase D (service_snapshot + pressure_sweep) confirmed that both host_1_1_1_1 and host_2_1_1_1 currently resolve web2.local→10.200.0.5 and web3.local→10.200.0.6 correctly from dns_server, successfully load HTTP 200 responses from those addresses (average ~4 ms), and that web_server_2 and web_server_3 answer HTTP on localhost. No stress-tool process, CPU saturation, or socket spike was found on any device. The reported inability to reach "web2.local" and "web3.local" from host_1_1_1_1 is not reproducible under current lab conditions and leaves no residual mechanism or trace (no flap script, no ACL remnant, no syslog evidence, no routing change). Root cause: no active fault — the helpdesk report describes a condition that is either fully resolved or was never present in this lab snapshot. No device requires restarting.
=== END ===